| parameters = {{Parameter Table
  | {{Parameter Row|name|The name of the object on TibiaWiki, which should be in most cases the same name of the page. If a page has disambiguation brackets, such as [[Giant Shimmering Pearl (Brown)]], this parameter should be the same. This parameter is used to retrieve the corresponding image gif file, and it's also very important in DPL tables.<br/><br/>This name should always use initial capitals using the same rules as the ones for [[TibiaWiki:Standards|page names]].|required=yes}}
  | {{Parameter Row|article|The article used for countable singular objects. It should only be one of 'a', 'an' or empty. The article 'the' should not be used, since when it exists it is actually part of the name. This parameter is used to properly build the look message.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|actualname|The name of the object as it appears in game when looked at. Most object names are all lower-case, however, some have upper-case initials when a proper name is mentioned, such as [[Vessel of Ferumbras]] (''vessel of Ferumbras''). Although this parameter is not required and the template will use the ''name'' in lower case instead, it's recommended to be added to avoid confusions and mistakes. This parameter is also used to build the look message.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|plural|The plural of the actualname parameter.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|itemid|The Object ID(s) of the object. The IDs can be found in the dat file, which can only be examined using specific tools. Multiple IDs can be used in one page if and only if all the other object properties are the same. In such cases, IDs should be given in a comma-separated list.<br/><br/>For instance, some walls or floor tiles are very similar, having the same name and same other properties, and creating one page for each would be tedious and repetitive, so a single page with all IDs is preferrable. If two tile objects are similar but have different ''mapcolor''s, on the other hand, it would be better to have them on different pages so the properties can be correctly displayed.|required=yes}}
  | {{Parameter Row|objectclass|The main "Class" of the object, as per TibiaWiki's [[Objects]] grouping. As per the [[TibiaWiki:Projects/Merge Items and Objects|infobox merge project]], however, the definition of classes and types are still under review.|required=yes}}
  | {{Parameter Row|primarytype|The main "Type" of the object, as per TibiaWiki's [[Objects]] grouping. As per the [[TibiaWiki:Projects/Merge Items and Objects|infobox merge project]], however, the definition of classes and types are still under review.|required=yes}}
  | {{Parameter Row|secondarytype|The secondary "Type" of the object, as per TibiaWiki's [[Objects]] grouping. As per the [[TibiaWiki:Projects/Merge Items and Objects|infobox merge project]], however, the definition of classes and types are still under review.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|tertiarytype|The tertiary "Type" of the object, as per TibiaWiki's [[Objects]] grouping. As per the [[TibiaWiki:Projects/Merge Items and Objects|infobox merge project]], however, the definition of classes and types are still under review.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|cooldown|The [[cooldown]] before the object can be used again.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|flavortext|Also known as 'description', this is the extra text that appears when looking at an object. Line breaks can be added, if necessary, using <nowiki><br/></nowiki>, but only if the line break also exists in the original description.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|words|If this item is a rune, set to the rune's displayed words (e.g. thunderstorm runes ("adori mas vis")).}}
  | {{Parameter Row|sounds|A list of {{Message|type=sound|sounds}} an object can make when interacted with. When at least one sound exists, the [[Template:Sound]] should be used, having each sound as a parameter. For example, on [[Stuffed Dragon]]:<br/><pre>| sounds        = {{Sound List|Fchhhhhh!|Zchhhhhh!|Groaaarrr.... *cough*|Aaa... CHOO!|You... will.... burn!!}}</pre><br/>Sounds are displayed under the Object's look message.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|implemented|The update version in which the object was implemented. This is a required parameter, since obviously all objects were implemented at some version, with some rare [[Updates/--|exceptions]] (objects that were/are only seen in [[Test Server]]s). Only numbers and dots should be used, i.e. ''12.20.8834''.|required=yes}}
  | {{Parameter Row|lightradius|If the object gives light, the radius of this light can be put here as an integer number.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|lightcolor|If the object gives light, the color value of this light can be given as an integer number. See [[Template:RGB Light Color]] for a full list.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|destructible|Use "yes" or "no" to indicate of the object is destructible, which means it can be destroyed by e.g. using a [[Melee]] weapon.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|immobile|Use 'yes' or 'no' to indicate if the Object cannot be moved around in the map. This is one of the most important parameters of the template in terms of object characterization. It should always be given, and can easily be verified in game or the client files.<br/><br/>It is important to remember that some objects, such as [[Store]] carpets, are ''immobile'', even though they can be transformed into mobile objects when used (in their rolled-up versions). For these cases, separate pages for each version of the carpet are necessary. |required=yes}}
  | {{Parameter Row|walkable|Whether or not an object can be walked over. All pickupable objects can be walked over (even though some have the ''blockspath'' property as well, which prevents map-clicking walking over them).}}
  | {{Parameter Row|walkingspeed|If it's a tile, the walking speed is how long it takes to cross the tile. Only use when walkable is set to "yes".}}
  | {{Parameter Row|unshootable|Use "yes" or "no" to indicate of the object is unshootable, in other words, if it blocks projectiles (distance weapons or runes) to be shot through.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|blockspath|Use "yes" or "no" to indicate of the object blocks the path.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|pickupable|Use 'yes' or 'no' to indicate if an object can be picked up, i.e., put into a container and carried by characters. [[:Category:Pickupable Objects|Pickupable Objects]] are popularly simply known as 'items', a distinction that was once the rule in TibiaWiki as well. This is however just a single property, and many properties are shared between non-pickupable and pickupable objects.<br/><br/>A pickupable object must also not be immobile, obviously. On the other hand, there are non-pickupable objects which can be moved, such as [[Furniture]]. Moreover, some of these movable non-pickupable items are ''wrappable'', which transform them into pickupable [[Furniture Kit]]s or [[Decoration Kit]]s. For these reasons, associating this parameter with others must be done with care to avoid wrong assumptions. |required=yes}}
  | {{Parameter Row|holdsliquid|Use "yes" or "no" to indicate of the object can hold liquid, which is mostly true for [[Liquid Containers]].}}
  | {{Parameter Row|usable|This simple parameter is used to inform whether or not the object can be "used", or simply interacted with. There are two different types of use interaction, "normal" use in which the action happens on the first click and "use-with" in which the interaction will be between the object and something else (another object, a character, the map, etc). Currently, there's no difference between them in TibiaWiki.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|writable|Use "yes" or "no" to indicate of the object can be written on, which is true for some documents.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|rewritable|Use "yes" or "no" to indicate of the object can be rewritten once it has been written.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|writechars|The amount of characters which can be written in the object.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|wrappable|Use "yes" or "no" to indicate if the object can be wrapped into a [[Furniture Kit]] or a [[Decoration Kit]].}}
  | {{Parameter Row|task_item|Use "yes" or "no" to indicate if the object is a task item (e.g. used for a delivery task). Case-insensitive. If omitted, it defaults to "no" and is not shown. When set to yes, the page is added to [[:Category:Task Items]].}}
  | {{Parameter Row|levelrequired|Minimum level to use the equipment and benefit from all of its perks. Note that some types of equipment can be equipped even if the character doesn't have the required level, however, in that case skill bonus and other properties won't work, the attack will be lowered, etc. If there is no level requirement, the parameter should be omitted.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|vocrequired|The object's vocation requirement. Use the text as displayed in-game, i.e. plural vocation names, commas to separate all except the last one which uses the text "and". If the object is used only by players with no vocation, use without. For example:
* [[Prismatic Legs]] - paladins
* [[Draken Boots]] - knights and paladins
* [[Great Mana Potion]] - sorcerers, druids and paladins
* [[Star Ring]] - without}}
  | {{Parameter Row|mlrequired|The object's magic level requirement. Must be used on all articles about [[Runes]]. If the magic level requirement for a rune is 0, set the parameter's value to 0.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|basepower|The object's base power. Created to be used on all articles about [[Runes]].}}
  | {{Parameter Row|hands|The amount of hands the object requires to be worn. Two or One. Include parameter only if the object is a weapon and is wielded in the weapon slot.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|weapontype|The weapon type of the object. Include if the object is a weapon and is wielded in the weapon slot. You can use:
* Axe
* Club
* Sword
* Fist
* Wand
* Rod
* Distance}}
  | {{Parameter Row|attack|The [[Physical Damage]] attack value of a weapon. Some weapons can have 'atk: 0', this should be explicit. Not to be used for wands and rods, there is a parameter for those.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|fire_attack|The [[Fire Damage]] attack value of a weapon, if it has any. Omit if the weapon doesn't deal this type of damage. Not to be used for wands and rods, there is a parameter for those.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|earth_attack|The [[Earth Damage]] attack value of a weapon, if it has any. Omit if the weapon doesn't deal this type of damage. Not to be used for wands and rods, there is a parameter for those.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|ice_attack|The [[Ice Damage]] attack value of a weapon, if it has any. Omit if the weapon doesn't deal this type of damage. Not to be used for wands and rods, there is a parameter for those.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|energy_attack|The [[Energy Damage]] attack value of a weapon, if it has any. Omit if the weapon doesn't deal this type of damage. Not to be used for wands and rods, there is a parameter for those.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|death_attack|The [[Death Damage]] attack value of a weapon, if it has any. Omit if the weapon doesn't deal this type of damage. Not to be used for wands and rods, there is a parameter for those.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|defense|The defense value of the object. Include if the object is a shield or weapon, omit otherwise.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|defensemod|The defense modifier value of the object. Include if the object's defense modifier is not 0; omit otherwise.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|imbueslots|The amount of available imbuing slots, value should be numeric and can be 1, 2 or 3.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|augments|The Augments which the object provides. Augments should be listed as they appear in the look message, without the parenthesis:<br/><br/><pre>| augments      = Eternal Winter -> Powerful Impact, Terra Wave -> Powerful Impact</pre>}}
  | {{Parameter Row|imbuements|A comma-separated list of all imbuements that require this object. This is '''NOT''' for objects that are imbuable, see '''imbueslots'''.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|upgradeclass|A number from 1 to 4 indicating the Classification of the item in the [[Exaltation Forge]] upgrade system.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|enchantable|Include if the object could be [[Enchanting|enchanted]] at Holy Shrines before [[Summer Update 2017]]; omit otherwise. Other forms of enchantment should not have this parameter, e.g. Rainbow Shield. If included, it must be set to yes.<br/><br/>This parameter is only kept for historical purposes, since we can keep a record of what was enchantable back in the day the system existed.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|enchanted|Include if the object was the result of enchanting. If included, it must be set to yes. Same status as ''enchantable''.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|range|The range of distance weapons, wands and rods. Should be an integer between 1 and 7? and omitted otherwise.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|atk_mod|The +atk modifier of the distance weapon. Only applies to distance since these weapons do not have a natural atk value; it comes from the ammunition. Include if the object is a distance weapon and the value isn't 0; omit otherwise.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|hit_mod|The +hit% modifier of the distance weapon. Only applies to distance since these weapons can miss their target. Include if the object is a distance weapon and the value isn't 0; omit otherwise.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|armor|The armor value of the object. Include this parameter only if the object has armor.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|resist|The elemental resistance of the object. Include this parameter only if the object has resistance to some element. Use the same format as in-game descriptions but without the leading "protection ", i.e.: physical +10%, energy +15%}}
  | {{Parameter Row|charges|The amount of charges which an amulet or necklace has when it is brand-new. Use integer values, like "5" or "100".}}
  | {{Parameter Row|crithit_ch|The intrisic [[Critical Hit]] chance of an object. Value should be a number and the % sign, as long as it isn't 0, e.g. '20%'. When provided, ''critextra_dmg'' must be provided as well.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|critextra_dmg|The intrisic [[Critical Hit]] damage of an object. Value should be a number and the % sign, as long as it isn't 0, e.g. '50%'. When provided, ''crithit_ch'' must be provided as well, even if it's 100%.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|manaleech_ch|The intrisic [[Mana Leech]] chance of an object. Value should be a number and the % sign, as long as it isn't 0, e.g. '100%'. When provided, ''manaleech_am'' must be provided as well.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|manaleech_am|The intrisic [[Mana Leech]] amount of an object. Value should be a number and the % sign, as long as it isn't 0, e.g. '2%'. When provided, ''manaleech_ch'' must be provided as well, even if it's 100%.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|hpleech_ch|Same as ''manaleech_ch'' but for [[Life Leech]] instead.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|hpleech_am|Same as ''manaleech_am'' but for [[Life Leech]] instead.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|attrib|The additional attributes of the object. Include the parameter only if the object uses it. Try to use other parameters first, resorting to attrib if none of them fit. Some examples are:
* distance fighting +3
* shielding -20}}
  | {{Parameter Row|weight|The weight of the object. Numbers with 2 decimal places only. Omit if the object cannot be picked up or doesn't have weight.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|stackable|Include if the object is stackable. Use "yes" if it is and "no" if it isn't (which is the default).}}
  | {{Parameter Row|marketable|Whether the item can be traded on the [[Market]], use "yes" or "no".}}
  | {{Parameter Row|consumable|Include if the object can be eaten or drunk (i.e. Meat); omit otherwise. If included, it should be set to yes.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|regenseconds|Include if the object can be eaten or drunk (i.e. Meat); omit otherwise. The number of seconds the food will regenerate health/mana for.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|hangable|Whether the object can be hung on walls or not, e.g. to decorate houses, use "yes" or "no".}}
  | {{Parameter Row|manacost|The amount of mana used when attacking with a wand, rod or rune. Include if the object is a wand, rod or a rune that requires mana to use such as [[Paralyse Rune]]. Positive integer numbers only.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|damagetype|The element when attacking with a wand, rod or attack rune. Include if the object is a wand, rod or attack rune (except [[Magic Wall Rune|Magic Wall]], [[Paralyse Rune|Paralyse]] and [[Wild Growth Rune|Wild Growth]] runes).}}
  | {{Parameter Row|damagerange|The damage range of the wand or rod. Include if the object is a magical wand or rod. Two positive integer numbers only, separated by a hyphen (e.g. 66-74).}}
  | {{Parameter Row|volume|The amount of objects that can be placed in a container. Include only if the object has volume. Positive integer numbers only.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|duration|The maximum time an expiring object can have. Include only if the object has a duration that is displayed on the object's description (e.g. a dwarven ring that will expire in 35 minutes and 18 seconds.).}}
  | {{Parameter Row|droppedby|A list of Creatures that drop this object using [[Template:Dropped By]]. Do not include classes of creatures, do not use plurals, do not use "Rareness" modifiers, for example use: '''<nowiki>{{Dropped By|Sibang}}.</nowiki>'''}}
  | {{Parameter Row|value|The approximate street value of the object. Keep in mind this can vary from server to server. Use numbers (100), number ranges (100-200), "Negotiable" (highly varying) or "Invaluable" (impossible to put a price on it), or "?" (unknown value).}}
  | {{Parameter Row|storevalue|The value of this object in the [[Store]] by using [[Template:Store Product]].}}
  | {{Parameter Row|npcvalue|The highest amount of gp the player can sell this object to an NPC for. Positive integer numbers only. Use 0 if the object cannot be sold to an NPC.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|npcprice|The lowest amount of gp the player can buy this object from an NPC for. Positive integer numbers only. Use 0 if the object cannot be bought from an NPC.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|pricecurrency|The currency used for items traded with anything but gold.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|npcvaluerook|The highest amount of gp the player can sell this object to a [[Rookgaard]] NPC for. Positive integer numbers only. Use 0 if the object cannot be sold to a Rookgaard NPC. Include only if this object can be found in Rookgaard; omit otherwise.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|npcpricerook|The lowest amount of gp the player can buy this object from a Rookgaard NPC for. Positive integer numbers only. Use 0 if the object cannot be bought from a Rookgaard NPC. Include only if this object can be found in Rookgaard; omit otherwise.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|buyfrom|A comma-separated list of NPCs who sell the object. If none, use "--". This only adds the category that the item is sold by an NPC. For configuring the actual table of prices, see https://tibia.fandom.com/wiki/Module:ItemPrices/data}}
  | {{Parameter Row|sellto|A list of NPCs who buy the object. If none, use "--". This only adds the category that the item is bought by an NPC. For configuring the actual table of prices, see https://tibia.fandom.com/wiki/Module:ItemPrices/data}}
  | {{Parameter Row|fansite|The name of the corresponding [[Fansite]], if this object is a [[Fansite Items|Fansite Item]]. When set, it is shown as the last entry under '''General Properties'''. Omit the parameter when the object is not associated with a fansite.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|rotatable|Use "yes" or "no" to indicate of the object can be rotated.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|mapcolor|The color value of the object on the [[Minimap]] can be given as an integer number. See [[Template:RGB Light Color]] for a full list.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|location|The location of the object, if it isn't commonly found.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|notes|General notes about the object, for example how if it's related to a quest, used to tame a creature, a very rare with interesting background, etc.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|notes2|Same as ''notes'', however, this part will not be transcluded in DPL tables. Should be used for longer notes such as those which have tables, long lists, several minimap templates, etc.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|history|Relevant historical information about the object, for example changes that were made to a weapon stats, or if the object became unobtainable at a certain update. The template should reflect the current in-game state of the object, but if something was different in the past it can be described here.}}
  | {{Parameter Row|status|The current status of the object, if it's not the default, which is ''active''. Possible values are:
  * ''deprecated'' means the object was completely removed from the client files. Note that if an object has become unobtainable, but still exists in the client (even if no player owns it or it cannot be found in the map), it's '''not''' deprecated.
  * ''event'' if the object can only be found during an event. Note that for items which are presistent after the event ends, such as drops from event creatures, should not have this status. It's purpuse is to indicate that the object can '''only''' be found if the event is active. 
  * ''unobtainable'' for objects which still exist in the game, but are not available anywhere, not even to be seen in Treasure Rooms. For example, the old [[Weapons of Destruction]] which still exist in the client files, but have all expired. Items such as the [[Golden Helmet]], which are posseded by players but exist in limited amounts, should ''not'' have this status. 
  * ''ts-only'' objects are those which only exist in [[Test Server]]s, such as the [[Test Voodoo Doll]].}}
 }}
